IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g1-interpretation`
IMPORT `g2-nouns`
IMPORT `g3-nouns`
IMPORT `g4-interpretation`
IMPORT `g5-interpretation`
IMPORT `g6-interpretation`
IMPORT `g7-interpretation`
IMPORT `g8-nouns`
IMPORT `g9-interpretation`

-- int-readings.l4: the readings of all nine groups, gathered in ONE record so that a headline function of the integration layer takes them as one ordinary GIVEN.
-- GENERATED by work/integrator/gen_readings.py from the nine `Interpretation of ...` records of the group modules (each field is set to the reading its group TYPICALLY takes).
-- Two readings are shared by several groups and must be one value (PLAN section (c), IP33 and IP35):
--   IP33  the meaning of the year of an annual return: G3 field `meaning of the year of an annual return` and G5 field `the meaning of the year of an annual return`;
--   IP35  the unit of a term of imprisonment: G6 F6.16, G7 F7.8, G8 F8.8 and G9 F9.13.
-- `Int the readings of the fleet` sets all six fields from the two shared values; a caller that wants another reading of any other fork builds that group's record itself (the group modules give one value per other reading).

§ `Integration layer -- the readings of the fleet`

DECLARE `Readings of the fleet` HAS
    `reading of Articles 1 and 2` IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` @desc The reading taken at each fork of Articles 1 and 2 (group G1)
    `reading of Articles 3 to 7` IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` @desc The reading taken at each fork of Articles 3 to 7 (group G2)
    `reading of Articles 8 to 10` IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10` @desc The reading taken at each fork of Articles 8 to 10 (group G3)
    `reading of Articles 11 and 12` IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 11 and 12` @desc The reading taken at each fork of Articles 11 and 12 (group G4)
    `reading of Articles 13 and 14` IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 13 and 14` @desc The reading taken at each fork of Articles 13 and 14 (group G5)
    `reading of Articles 15 to 20` IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 15 to 20` @desc The reading taken at each fork of Articles 15 to 20 (group G6)
    `reading of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes` IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes` @desc The reading taken at each fork of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes (group G7)
    `reading of Articles 26 to 36` IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 26 to 36` @desc The reading taken at each fork of Articles 26 to 36 (group G8)
    `reading of Schedules 1 and 2` IS AN `Interpretation of Schedules 1 and 2` @desc The reading taken at each fork of Schedules 1 and 2 (group G9)
    `meaning of the year of an annual return` IS A `Meaning of the year of an annual return` @desc IP33: the one reading of the year for the annual return that groups G3 (Article 8(3)(j)) and G5 (Articles 13(7), 13(9)(a)) both use
    `unit of a term of imprisonment` IS A `Unit of a term of imprisonment` @desc IP35: the one unit (calendar months or days) in which the terms of imprisonment of groups G6, G7, G8 and G9 are measured

-- Group G1: Interpretation of Articles 1 and 2 (module g1-interpretation), every fork as that group takes it.
GIVETH AN `Interpretation of Articles 1 and 2`
`Int the reading of Articles 1 and 2` MEANS
    `Interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` WITH
        `ranges and sub-paragraph (ba)` IS `the ranges follow the letters of the amended list, so (ba) is inside (a) to (h)`
        `limbs of Article 2(10)(b)` IS `every limb (i) to (vi) needs the offence to be in relation to a charity or an equivalent entity`
        `constitutional Law of (g) and (h)` IS `none, because Article 2(5) names no Law for sub-paragraphs (g) and (h)`
        `cases for a body in more than one kind` IS `every case of Article 2(4) to (7) that applies`
        `meaning of published` IS `the opinion of the person publishing`
        `reach of in relation to Jersey` IS `only the Royal Charter in sub-paragraph (iii)`
        `time of the standing of a charity` IS `when the conduct in Article 2(10) occurred`
        `overlap of sub-paragraph (g)` IS `as written, so a foundation or an incorporated 1862 association is also within (g)`

-- Group G2: Interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 (module g2-nouns), every fork as that group takes it.
GIVETH AN `Interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
`Int the reading of Articles 3 to 7` MEANS
    `Interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` WITH
        `how the purposes of an entity are tested` IS `at least one charitable purpose is required, and an ancillary purpose counts only beside one`
        `how acting in that capacity qualifies the persons named in Article 5(2)` IS `the person must be permitted to act as a Minister, a member of the States Assembly or an equivalent`
        `what a Minister means in Article 5(2)(a)` IS `any Minister of the Government of Jersey`
        `how a standard of promptness is measured` IS `by an input judgement that the time taken was reasonable or practicable`
        `which head a philosophical belief falls within` IS `paragraph (1)(p), by the analogy that Article 6(2)(f) states`
        `how the days of a measured period are counted` IS `the day of the event is not counted, so the day after it is the first day`
        `how before issuing or amending guidance is read` IS `the consultation and the report must fall on an earlier day than the day the guidance is issued or amended`
        `whether the examples in Article 4(3) add to Article 4(2)` IS `the examples illustrate Article 4(2) and are bound by its conditions`
        `how so far as reasonably practicable qualifies Article 4(4)` IS `each limb binds so far as it appeared reasonably practicable`
        `what follows from a determination made in breach of the duties on its maker` IS `the determination does not answer the question`
        `how equality and diversity is read` IS `a purpose must promote both equality and diversity`
        `which guidance Articles 5(6) to 5(8) apply to` IS `the guidance under Article 5(4), including the guidance on public benefit that Article 7(4) requires it to contain`
        `whether the Commissioner's staff exercising the Commissioner's function are bound` IS `a member of staff exercising a function of the Commissioner under Schedule 1 paragraph 4(3) is bound as the Commissioner is`
        `how Article 6(2)(e) is read` IS `Article 6(2)(e) is declaratory: relief given by accommodation or care is within paragraph (1)(n) only as relief of those in need`

-- Group G3: Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10 (module g3-nouns), every fork as that group takes it; the shared field is set from the argument.
GIVEN year IS A `Meaning of the year of an annual return` @desc IP33: the meaning of the year of an annual return
GIVETH AN `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10`
`Int the reading of Articles 8 to 10` year MEANS
    `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10` WITH
        `start of the ten years of retention` IS `from the day the Commissioner receives or makes each copy`
        `meaning of the year of an annual return` IS year
        `reach of Article 10(4)` IS `a registered charity is an entity entered in the general or the restricted section only`
        `counting the day of an event in a period of years` IS `the day of the event is not counted, so the last day of the period is the anniversary`
        `adding a year to a date that does not exist` IS `the date moves back to the last day of the month`
        `day on which an entry takes effect` IS `on the day of the entry`
        `the most recent year` IS `the latest year that has ended before the day asked`
        `required steps notices noted` IS `every notice that has been served`
        `entities within Article 8(4)(a)` IS `an entity that its constitutional Law requires to have a registered office or business address in Jersey`
        `main premises that are a private dwelling house` IS `Article 8(4)(b) does not apply, so Article 8(4)(c) is reached`
        `section that decides Article 8(5)(b)` IS `the section the entity was entered in immediately before deregistration`
        `who must meet a condition under Article 9(2)` IS `whoever makes the request, an applicant for registration or a registered charity`
        `reach of Article 8(3)(a) to sub-paragraph (ba)` IS `Article 8(3)(a) reaches only the sub-paragraphs it names`

-- Group G4: Interpretation of Articles 11 and 12 (module g4-interpretation), every fork as that group takes it.
GIVETH AN `Interpretation of Articles 11 and 12`
`Int the reading of Articles 11 and 12` MEANS
    `Interpretation of Articles 11 and 12` WITH
        `how the twelve months preceding the application are counted` IS `the twelve months ending on the day before the application`
        `which day is the date of the application` IS `the day the application is lodged`
        `what an application that does not comply leads to` IS `no duty to register or to refuse arises while the application does not comply`
        `how the duty to register meets the bars on granting the application` IS `a bar on granting the application displaces the duty to register`
        `whether a formerly registered charity is another registered charity` IS `a formerly registered charity is not another registered charity`
        `how a year is taken back from 29 February` IS `a year before 29 February is 28 February`
        `which names of another registered charity Article 12(1)(a) compares` IS `its registered name and its alternative registered names`
        `whether a previous registered name is still one of its registered names` IS `a previous registered name is not one of its registered names`
        `how the period for the Commissioner's decision is counted` IS `the period starts the day after the date of the application`
        `how reasonable time and as soon as practicable are read for the guidance` IS `as a determination the caller supplies`
        `which payees Article 11(2)(e)(ii) reaches` IS `a payee who was a governor when the payment was made`
        `how applies or should be applied is read in Article 11(4)(f)` IS `a ground of mandatory refusal applies, or a ground of discretionary refusal should be applied`

-- Group G5: Interpretation of Articles 13 and 14 (module g5-interpretation), every fork as that group takes it; the shared field is set from the argument.
GIVEN year IS A `Meaning of the year of an annual return` @desc IP33: the meaning of the year of an annual return
GIVETH AN `Interpretation of Articles 13 and 14`
`Int the reading of Articles 13 and 14` year MEANS
    `Interpretation of Articles 13 and 14` WITH
        `how promptness is measured` IS `an input judgement that the report was made promptly`
        `the meaning of the year of an annual return` IS year
        `the meaning of an Order under paragraph (8)` IS `the Order under paragraph (7) as extended by paragraph (8)`
        `the meaning of misconduct in the administration` IS `misconduct within Article 2(10) that bears on the administration of the charity`
        `whether a return sent on the due date is timely` IS `timely if sent on or before the due date`
        `whether the day deregistration takes effect is inside the registration` IS `outside: registered up to the day before deregistration takes effect`
        `the meaning of a purpose that is not charitable` IS `any purpose that is not a charitable purpose under Article 6, a purely ancillary purpose included`
        `how the two paragraphs of Article 13(5) combine` IS `either the original condition, or after a prior permission and a cessation the different condition`
        `whether the first day counts in a period fixed by the court` IS `the first day named is the first day of the period`
        `whether the day of the event counts in a number of days` IS `the day of the event is not counted: the last prompt day is the event day plus the number of days`
        `the anniversary of a registration made on 29 February` IS `the last day of February (the day is clamped, as daydate add years does)`
        `the purposes an order under Article 14(2) must serve` IS `at least one of the three purposes`
        `the date on which a matter arises` IS `the date of the event or proposal`
        `the statement a payment must be consistent with` IS `the statement in force on the day of the payment`

-- Group G6: Interpretation of Articles 15 to 20 (module g6-interpretation), every fork as that group takes it; the shared field is set from the argument.
GIVEN unit IS A `Unit of a term of imprisonment` @desc IP35: the unit of a term of imprisonment
GIVETH AN `Interpretation of Articles 15 to 20`
`Int the reading of Articles 15 to 20` unit MEANS
    `Interpretation of Articles 15 to 20` WITH
        `what follows where the entity has not complied with Article 15(2)` IS `no duty arises under Article 15(3)`
        `how Article 16(2) relates to the procedure of Article 16(1)` IS `Article 16(2) governs alone and the duty arises on satisfaction with no prior notice`
        `which notice Articles 17(2)(c) and 17(4) mean` IS `the notice by which the Commissioner deregisters`
        `the date before which property must have been acquired to be remaining property` IS `acquired before the date from which the termination takes effect`
        `when the ten years of Article 17(1)(a) start` IS `the ten years run from the date of the deregistration notice`
        `how long the bar on assigning the registered number lasts` IS `the bar on assigning the registered number has no end`
        `which governors Article 18(2) binds` IS `only the governors of unincorporated bodies within Article 2(1)(i)`
        `what the reasonable time of Article 18(4)(d)(ii) qualifies` IS `the reasonable time qualifies only the failure to take proper steps`
        `whether a disqualification that has ended is a reportable matter` IS `a disqualification counts although it has ended`
        `when the ban of Article 19(10) starts` IS `the ban starts on the report to the Commissioner`
        `whether acting in breach of Article 19(2) or (4) is an offence` IS `Article 19(11) reaches only paragraph (10)`
        `how a report is judged prompt under Article 19(2)` IS `promptness is a determination supplied as an input`
        `whether the time for objections must be reasonable` IS `the time specified must be reasonable or the deregistration is not authorised`
        `how the fifteen years of Article 20(5) are counted` IS `the last day is the anniversary, and 29 February falls back to 28 February`
        `how the duty in Article 19(9)(e)(i) stands against Article 28(3)` IS `Article 28(3) prevails and no duty to require removal arises for an organized religious charity`
        `how a term of imprisonment of one year or two years is measured` IS unit
        `when the Commissioner may deregister after giving the preliminary notice` IS `the Commissioner may deregister only after the last day for objections`
        `how the ten years of Article 17(1)(a) are counted` IS `the last day is the anniversary, and 29 February falls back to 28 February`
        `when the entity has failed to comply with a required steps notice` IS `the notice has not been complied with once the time it names has ended without the steps taken`
        `whether a declaration given on the day of the application is in time` IS `a declaration given on the day of the application is in time`
        `from when a governor who has been notified is in breach of Article 19(4)` IS `the governor is in breach from the day after the notification`
        `whether the last day named in a time limit is inside the permission` IS `the day named is the last day of the permission`
        `whose view of expediency lets a person apply under Article 20(3)` IS `only the applicant's own view that it is expedient`
        `whether assisting another governor is misconduct only if that governor engages in misconduct` IS `the assisting or encouraging is misconduct only if the other governor engages in misconduct`

-- Group G7: Interpretation of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes (module g7-interpretation), every fork as that group takes it; the shared field is set from the argument.
GIVEN unit IS A `Unit of a term of imprisonment` @desc IP35: the unit of a term of imprisonment
GIVETH AN `Interpretation of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes`
`Int the reading of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes` unit MEANS
    `Interpretation of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes` WITH
        `how a day on which a text takes effect at a stated time is treated` IS `a question about that day alone is refused`
        `how “7 days after it is made” is counted` IS `the day of making is left out`
        `the numbering the commencement table speaks in` IS `the table is in the original numbers`
        `how the strict and the knowing offences combine for one act` IS `both offences are made out`
        `the wording of the advantage limb of the knowing offences` IS `the wording differs as printed`
        `the bodies within Article 37(1)` IS `only partnerships and bodies corporate`
        `the date on which a notice is served` IS `the date of receipt`
        `the unit of a term of imprisonment` IS unit
        `how a Part brought into force in two stages is treated` IS `in force when all its Articles are`
        `how capacity is paired with the kind of body in Article 37(1)` IS `capacity as printed for each kind of body`
        `how the day named as the day of commencement is counted` IS `the named day is the first day in force`
        `whether Article 22 defines an excepted foreign charity outside Article 21` IS `Article 22 defines the term wherever the Law uses it`
        `whether adapting Articles 21 to 23 under Article 24(3)(a) can carry their imprisonment` IS `the cap of Article 24(4) applies to every offence of the Regulations`
        `whether an Order under Article 2(2) can make consequential amendments of other provisions of the Law` IS `only Regulations can make consequential amendments of this Law`

-- Group G8: Interpretation of Articles 26 to 36 (module g8-nouns), every fork as that group takes it; the shared field is set from the argument.
GIVEN unit IS A `Unit of a term of imprisonment` @desc IP35: the unit of a term of imprisonment
GIVETH AN `Interpretation of Articles 26 to 36`
`Int the reading of Articles 26 to 36` unit MEANS
    `Interpretation of Articles 26 to 36` WITH
        `when the retention year of Article 26(5) starts` IS `the year of Article 26(5) runs from the day the document is provided or retained`
        `how promptness under Article 26(6) is judged` IS `promptness under Article 26(6) is a judgement the caller supplies`
        `whether Article 28(1)(a) reaches a philosophical belief purpose` IS `only a purpose within Article 6(1)(c) counts under Article 28(1)(a)`
        `whether the list of appealable decisions in Article 33 is closed` IS `the list of appealable decisions in Article 33 is closed`
        `on what ground a decision of the tribunal is appealed to the court` IS `a decision of the tribunal is appealed to the court only on the ground in Article 35(1)`
        `from when an appeal time limit under Article 36(2) runs` IS `an appeal time limit under Article 36(2) runs from the notice of the decision`
        `how a period fixed by a notice under Article 26 or 27 is counted` IS `the day of service is not counted in a period fixed by a notice`
        `unit of the terms of imprisonment in Articles 26 and 29` IS unit
        `where the retention year of Article 26(5) ends` IS `the year of Article 26(5) ends on the anniversary of the day it starts`
        `how a year is added to 29 February under Article 26(5)` IS `a year of Article 26(5) from 29 February ends on 28 February`
        `which consents Article 29(1) requires` IS `Article 29(1) requires both consents`
        `whether the first day counts in an appeal time limit under Article 36(2)` IS `the day of the anchor is not counted in an appeal time limit`
        `who is excluded from appealing under Article 33(5)` IS `any applicant for registration or registered charity is excluded from appealing under Article 33(5)`
        `what Article 27(1) requires of the Commissioner's belief` IS `the Commissioner's belief alone is the ground under Article 27(1)`
        `which notices may require a governor to be suspended, removed or replaced` IS `only a notice under Article 27(1)(c) or (d) may require a governor to be suspended, removed or replaced`
        `whether Article 33(2)(a) reaches a deregistration on the charity's own application` IS `Article 33(2)(a) reaches a deregistration granted on the charity's own application`
        `when a person must have been a governor to fall within Article 26(2)(b)` IS `a governor at any time of an entity registered at any time falls within Article 26(2)(b)`
        `how the two grounds of Article 33(5) combine with the two times` IS `each ground of Article 33(5) must hold at both times`
        `which charity Article 26(4)(a) speaks of` IS `the registered charity of Article 26(4)(a) is a charity registered now`

-- Group G9: Interpretation of Schedules 1 and 2 (module g9-interpretation), every fork as that group takes it; the shared field is set from the argument.
GIVEN unit IS A `Unit of a term of imprisonment` @desc IP35: the unit of a term of imprisonment
GIVETH AN `Interpretation of Schedules 1 and 2`
`Int the reading of Schedules 1 and 2` unit MEANS
    `Interpretation of Schedules 1 and 2` WITH
        `the 2 weeks before an appointment` IS `the appointment is 14 or more days after the notice`
        `the 6 years of an appointment` IS `the end date is the day the term expires`
        `a resignation on notice` IS `the office ends when the notice period runs out, the months being clamped`
        `an absence from duties` IS `the days of absence are counted, the first and the last included`
        `the 2 weeks after a termination` IS `the 14th day after the termination day is in time`
        `twelve years of service` IS `twelve calendar years measured in days from the first day of service`
        `the 4 months after the end of the year` IS `the months are added and the day is clamped to the end of the month`
        `the decision under Article 15(3)` IS `both outcomes of the decision are reserved`
        `a cost directed to the Fund` IS `the Fund bears the cost in place of the annual income of the States`
        `as soon as practicable` IS `as soon as practicable is a judgement supplied as an input`
        `service as a designated relevant person` IS `service as a designated relevant person does not count`
        `a year in which the office was held for only part of it` IS `a report is required for the part of the year in which the office was held`
        `the unit of the cap on imprisonment` IS unit
        `before appointing` IS `the views were sought on an earlier day than the day of the appointment`
        `a vacant office of chair or vice-chair` IS `a vacant office counts as absent`
        `the decision on entry in the restricted section` IS `it is not reserved because it is not a decision under Article 11`
        `membership of the States when appointed` IS `only becoming a member during the appointment ends it`
        `the responsible officer where several members of staff are available` IS `the one member of staff the Minister has named is the responsible officer`
        `the ground of absence for terminating an appointment` IS `the Minister's satisfaction and the absence longer than the number of weeks are both required`

-- The readings of the fleet, from the two shared values.
GIVEN year IS A `Meaning of the year of an annual return` @desc IP33: the meaning of the year of an annual return, set in both G3 and G5
      unit IS A `Unit of a term of imprisonment` @desc IP35: the unit of a term of imprisonment, set in G6, G7, G8 and G9
GIVETH A `Readings of the fleet`
`Int the readings of the fleet` year unit MEANS
    `Readings of the fleet` WITH
        `reading of Articles 1 and 2` IS (`Int the reading of Articles 1 and 2`)
        `reading of Articles 3 to 7` IS (`Int the reading of Articles 3 to 7`)
        `reading of Articles 8 to 10` IS (`Int the reading of Articles 8 to 10` year)
        `reading of Articles 11 and 12` IS (`Int the reading of Articles 11 and 12`)
        `reading of Articles 13 and 14` IS (`Int the reading of Articles 13 and 14` year)
        `reading of Articles 15 to 20` IS (`Int the reading of Articles 15 to 20` unit)
        `reading of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes` IS (`Int the reading of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes` unit)
        `reading of Articles 26 to 36` IS (`Int the reading of Articles 26 to 36` unit)
        `reading of Schedules 1 and 2` IS (`Int the reading of Schedules 1 and 2` unit)
        `meaning of the year of an annual return` IS year
        `unit of a term of imprisonment` IS unit

-- The readings every group takes by default: the calendar year, calendar months.
GIVETH A `Readings of the fleet`
`Int the favoured readings of the fleet` MEANS
    `Int the readings of the fleet` `the calendar year` `calendar months`

-- IP33 and IP35 hold: the six fields that must be one value are one value.
GIVEN readings IS A `Readings of the fleet` @desc The readings of the fleet
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Int the readings of the fleet are consistent` readings MEANS
        (readings's `reading of Articles 8 to 10`)'s `meaning of the year of an annual return` EQUALS readings's `meaning of the year of an annual return`
    AND (readings's `reading of Articles 13 and 14`)'s `the meaning of the year of an annual return` EQUALS readings's `meaning of the year of an annual return`
    AND (readings's `reading of Articles 15 to 20`)'s `how a term of imprisonment of one year or two years is measured` EQUALS readings's `unit of a term of imprisonment`
    AND (readings's `reading of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes`)'s `the unit of a term of imprisonment` EQUALS readings's `unit of a term of imprisonment`
    AND (readings's `reading of Articles 26 to 36`)'s `unit of the terms of imprisonment in Articles 26 and 29` EQUALS readings's `unit of a term of imprisonment`
    AND (readings's `reading of Schedules 1 and 2`)'s `the unit of the cap on imprisonment` EQUALS readings's `unit of a term of imprisonment`

